  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25146288",
      "title": "Adding The Contact API Route",
      "lectureOrder": 373,
      "videoOrder": 344,
      "sourceHash": "0cb4828b8abad9fb2e56038d74ff7dfca8a418681189b15051882f04201e29de",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 4.02,
          "en": "So let's add the API route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.02,
          "end": 5.71,
          "en": "to what you want to talk here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.71,
          "end": 8.49,
          "en": "You learned that API routes are added by going",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.49,
          "end": 12.48,
          "en": "to the pages folder and then in there, the API folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.48,
          "end": 15.84,
          "en": "and then in there, the contact.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.84,
          "end": 17.53,
          "en": "Now, that file name is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.53,
          "end": 20.89,
          "en": "but this leads to a route of /api/contact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.89,
          "end": 24.313,
          "en": "to which we can send requests to reach this API route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.33,
          "end": 27.71,
          "en": "Now in there, we should just set up a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.71,
          "end": 30.78,
          "en": "typically called handler, which is exported,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.78,
          "end": 31.613,
          "en": "and hence, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.613,
          "end": 33.64,
          "en": "the function name doesn't actually matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.6,
          "end": 35.93,
          "en": "This function, as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.93,
          "end": 38.35,
          "en": "receives a request and a response object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.35,
          "end": 41.05,
          "en": "and it only executes on the server-side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.05,
          "end": 44.63,
          "en": "It's never included in any client-side code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.63,
          "end": 48.24,
          "en": "and here we can then handle the incoming request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.24,
          "end": 51.84,
          "en": "check the request method, extract data from the request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.84,
          "end": 53.69,
          "en": "and do whatever we need to do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.69,
          "end": 55.63,
          "en": "and that's what I'll do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.63,
          "end": 59.63,
          "en": "I'll first of all, check if request method is equal to POST,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.63,
          "end": 62.79,
          "en": "because I want to submit this contact form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 62.79,
          "end": 64.68,
          "en": "with a POST request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 64.68,
          "end": 67.1,
          "en": "So any other requests will be ignored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 67.1,
          "end": 68.713,
          "en": "and will not do anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 69.57,
          "end": 73.76,
          "en": "So if the request method is POST, then we'll continue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 73.76,
          "end": 76.24,
          "en": "As a first step, I want to extract data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 76.24,
          "end": 78.33,
          "en": "from the body of that request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 78.33,
          "end": 81.3,
          "en": "Now, thankfully, as we learned, Next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 81.3,
          "end": 84.24,
          "en": "will automatically parse that body for us,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 84.24,
          "end": 87.19,
          "en": "so we have this request body property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 87.19,
          "end": 89.56,
          "en": "which holds the request body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 89.56,
          "end": 92.06,
          "en": "and we can now just get data out of that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 92.06,
          "end": 94.81,
          "en": "for example, with object de-structuring,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 94.81,
          "end": 98.89,
          "en": "and we could expect that we have a email,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 98.89,
          "end": 101.7,
          "en": "a name, and a message field in that body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 101.7,
          "end": 104.47,
          "en": "We have to make sure that we add those fields",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 104.47,
          "end": 107.18,
          "en": "to the request body when we send the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 107.18,
          "end": 109.16,
          "en": "from the front-end later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 109.16,
          "end": 112.11,
          "en": "but here I'll assume that I have a email,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 112.11,
          "end": 115.90299999999999,
          "en": "a name, and a message property in my request body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 117.05,
          "end": 119.97,
          "en": "Now we can validate that, because you learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 119.97,
          "end": 123.69,
          "en": "that you should not trust client-side validation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 123.69,
          "end": 127.15,
          "en": "because that can always be disabled or tricked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 127.15,
          "end": 130.5,
          "en": "So here I then check if we don't have a email,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 130.5,
          "end": 135.06,
          "en": "or email does not include a at sign",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 135.06,
          "end": 137.3,
          "en": "by adding a exclamation mark here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 137.3,
          "end": 139.72,
          "en": "or we don't have a name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 139.72,
          "end": 144.72,
          "en": "or if we trim the name it's equal to an empty string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 144.93,
          "end": 147.57999999999998,
          "en": "or we don't have a message,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 147.57999999999998,
          "end": 152.57999999999998,
          "en": "or if we trim message, it's an empty string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.46,
          "end": 156.7,
          "en": "If either of these conditions is met",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 156.7,
          "end": 158.41,
          "en": "then we don't continue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 158.41,
          "end": 161.36,
          "en": "Then I'll return to stop function execution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.36,
          "end": 163.02,
          "en": "and I'll send back a response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 163.02,
          "end": 166.74,
          "en": "with that response object, as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 166.74,
          "end": 169.49,
          "en": "There we can call status to set a status code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 169.49,
          "end": 173.05,
          "en": "and set this to 422, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 173.05,
          "end": 175.73,
          "en": "and then I'll do call JSON on that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 175.73,
          "end": 178.68,
          "en": "to add some data in JSON format,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 178.68,
          "end": 182.8,
          "en": "which is the defacto standard format for exchanging data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 182.8,
          "end": 186.35,
          "en": "with APIs, to add some data to the response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 186.35,
          "end": 188.05,
          "en": "and here we pass a object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 188.05,
          "end": 190.54,
          "en": "where we could add a message property and say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 190.54,
          "end": 194.193,
          "en": "invalid input, something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.09,
          "end": 198.89,
          "en": "Okay, now, if we make it past this if check,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 198.89,
          "end": 200.94,
          "en": "we have valid data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 200.94,
          "end": 204.36,
          "en": "and then we want to store it in a database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 204.36,
          "end": 207.71,
          "en": "Now that will be step number two, for the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 207.71,
          "end": 210.67000000000002,
          "en": "I'll just add a new message object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 210.67000000000002,
          "end": 215.67000000000002,
          "en": "and just add my email, name, and message here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 216,
          "end": 217.95,
          "en": "and then just console.log it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 217.95,
          "end": 220.82999999999998,
          "en": "but later we will also store it in a database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 220.82999999999998,
          "end": 224.42000000000002,
          "en": "just as we did it before in the course already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 224.42000000000002,
          "end": 226.32999999999998,
          "en": "but for the moment, that's it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 226.32999999999998,
          "end": 229.3,
          "en": "and of course, I'll send back a response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 229.3,
          "end": 232.37,
          "en": "where I set the status code to 201,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 232.37,
          "end": 235.82999999999998,
          "en": "which means that it was a success and we added a resource.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 235.82999999999998,
          "end": 237.49,
          "en": "We stored the message,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 237.49,
          "end": 239.77,
          "en": "even though technically we didn't yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 239.77,
          "end": 243.223,
          "en": "and then maybe also a message here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 244.32,
          "end": 247.61,
          "en": "successfully stored message,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 247.61,
          "end": 251.82,
          "en": "and also, maybe send back the message if we want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 251.82,
          "end": 252.89,
          "en": "It's of course, up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 252.89,
          "end": 254.963,
          "en": "which kind of data you want to send back,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 255.81,
          "end": 258.4,
          "en": "and with that, we're done with that API route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 258.4,
          "end": 260.45,
          "en": "Now, before we connect the database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 260.45,
          "end": 263.1,
          "en": "let's make sure we do add the front-end code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 263.1,
          "end": 264.89300000000003,
          "en": "for sending requests to it.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
